    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d745">

                <pb facs="0683" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg567"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.51/204A.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister of
                        Honduras</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-02-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 11, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: Referring to my note of
                    the 8th instant, and to our conversation of yesterday, it gives me pleasure to
                    transmit to you the final copies of the bankers’ and fiscal agent contracts
                    relating to the proposed Honduran loan. I am glad to be able to inform you that
                    the Department is now in receipt of a favorable report from the attorneys who
                    were requested by the Department to examine the contracts from the standpoint of
                    Honduras.</p>
                <p>The attorney for the bankers informs the Department, in a letter dated yesterday,
                    that these agreements are now satisfactory to the bankers and that they are
                    prepared to execute the same whenever you are ready to do so.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
